<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 27 August, from 479 BCE to 1939.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/479-bce">479 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,504 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Greeks defeat the Persian army at Plataea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Greek alliance led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> defeated the Persian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardonius">Mardonius</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a>, on a date traditionally placed in late August. The victory ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>'s invasion of mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1232">1232 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">794 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hōjō Yasutoki issues the Goseibai Shikimoku legal code</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hōjō Yasutoki, third shikken (regent) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>, promulgated the Goseibai Shikimoku, or Formulary of Adjudications, the shogunate's legal code. It was the first Japanese legal code governing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> class.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">Samurai</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1593">1593 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">433 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pierre Barrière's attempt to assassinate Henry IV fails</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pierre Barrière's attempt to assassinate King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a> failed when a Dominican priest to whom he had confessed denounced him. Barrière was executed on 31 August.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1600">1600 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">426 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ishida Mitsunari's Western Army besieges Fushimi Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishida-mitsunari">Ishida Mitsunari</a>'s Western Army laid siege to Fushimi Castle, held for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> by a much smaller garrison under Torii Mototada. The castle fell, but its resistance bought Ieyasu time to regroup and eventually win the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishida-mitsunari">Ishida Mitsunari</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British forces defeat Washington at the Battle of Long Island</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General William Howe outflanked and routed the Continental Army in Brooklyn, the largest battle of the war. Two nights later Washington's army escaped across the East River.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leopold II and Frederick William II issue the Declaration of Pillnitz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Pillnitz near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-ii-of-prussia">Frederick William II of Prussia</a> and Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Leopold II</a> declared their joint support for King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. The declaration agitated French revolutionaries and helped bring on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-first-coalition">War of the First Coalition</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Leopold II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-ii-of-prussia">Frederick William II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1859">1859 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">167 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edwin Drake strikes oil in Pennsylvania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Drilling near Titusville, Edwin Drake's well struck oil at about 21 metres. It was the first commercially successful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oil-well">oil well</a> in the US and launched the modern petroleum industry.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1928">1928 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">98 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fifteen nations sign the Kellogg-Briand Pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Signatories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> renounced war as an instrument of national policy. The pact had no means of enforcement, but it later underpinned charges of crimes against peace at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Heinkel He 178 makes the first jet-powered flight</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Test pilot Erich Warsitz flew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinkel">Heinkel</a> He 178 at Rostock-Marienehe, the first flight of an aircraft powered by a turbojet. Days later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
